CPMS query: accept whitespace between fields without consuming malformed replies

MOLY replies include spaces around the separators. Match the complete nine-field
response, keep quoted storage names bounded, and accept multi-digit final counts.
Unknown storage-name handling and the unused receive-storage behavior stay intact.

Only current-storage parsing is changed; this is not an SMS transport fix.

--- a/src/mm-modem-helpers.c
+++ b/src/mm-modem-helpers.c
@@ -3178,7 +3178,11 @@
  * +CPMS: <memr>,<usedr>,<totalr>,<memw>,<usedw>,<totalw>, <mems>,<useds>,<totals>
  */
 
-#define CPMS_QUERY_REGEX "\\+CPMS:\\s*\"(?P<memr>.*)\",[0-9]+,[0-9]+,\"(?P<memw>.*)\",[0-9]+,[0-9]+,\"(?P<mems>.*)\",[0-9]+,[0-9]"
+#define CPMS_QUERY_REGEX \
+    "^\\s*\\+CPMS:\\s*" \
+    "\"(?P<memr>[^\"\\r\\n]+)\"\\s*,\\s*[0-9]+\\s*,\\s*[0-9]+\\s*,\\s*" \
+    "\"(?P<memw>[^\"\\r\\n]+)\"\\s*,\\s*[0-9]+\\s*,\\s*[0-9]+\\s*,\\s*" \
+    "\"(?P<mems>[^\"\\r\\n]*)\"\\s*,\\s*[0-9]+\\s*,\\s*[0-9]+\\s*$"
 
 gboolean
 mm_3gpp_parse_cpms_query_response (const gchar *reply,
